```
$ jci-coverage upload --help
Standalone: takes a coverage file path and uploads it. Does not
require `report`, Rust, or `cargo-llvm-cov` — the caller is
responsible for the file existing at the given path in a format
OtterWise accepts. It must run in CircleCI: OtterWise shows only
uploads that carry a CI identity, so elsewhere it refuses unless told
to upload anyway (see the allow-local option).

Usage: jci-coverage upload [OPTIONS] --file <PATH>

Options:
      --file <PATH>
          Path to the coverage report to upload

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

      --repo-token <TOKEN>
          Repository token.
          
          Falls back to `OTTERWISE_TOKEN` when omitted.

      --endpoint <URL>
          Override the upload endpoint (primarily for testing)

      --allow-local
          Upload even when not running in CircleCI.
          
          OtterWise shows only uploads that carry a CI identity: from
          anywhere else it answers "Queued for processing" and the
          result never appears. Without this flag `upload` refuses to
          run outside CircleCI (`CIRCLECI` is not `true`).

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```
